# GLM-5.3-Flash EXL3 — 2× DGX Spark (GB10 / SM121)
# Copy to .env and edit. ./start.sh does this for you on first run.

# --- nodes (edit these) ------------------------------------------------
HEAD_IP=10.0.0.1
WORKER_IP=10.0.0.2
# SSH user on the worker. Unset = same as the user running ./start.sh.
# Only set this when the worker account differs (e.g. WORKER_USER=zurih).
# WORKER_USER=
# WORKER_HOME=/home/zurih
# WORKER_SSH=zurih@10.0.0.2

# Direct CX7 QSFP (spark1 f1 ↔ spark2 f0 on this kit). NCCL cannot use the
# 10.0.0.x loopback aliases — without these pins ncclCommInitRank hangs.
# Other kits: names differ (e.g. enP2p1s0f1np1/roceP2p1s0f1 on both nodes of
# some Spark pairs) — list yours with `ls /sys/class/infiniband` + `ip -br a`.
# These per-node values are what the containers get; exporting generic
# NCCL_SOCKET_IFNAME / NCCL_IB_HCA does NOT override them.
HEAD_CX7_IF=enp1s0f1np1
WORKER_CX7_IF=enp1s0f0np0
HEAD_CX7_IB=rocep1s0f1
WORKER_CX7_IB=rocep1s0f0
# The RoCEv2 GID index is per-NIC: each node needs the index carrying its OWN
# ::ffff:<ip> entry. An all-zero entry kills that rank ~60 s in (ibv_modify_qp
# errno 61); preflight verifies each rank against its own device. Inspect:
#   cat /sys/class/infiniband/<dev>/ports/1/gids/{0..7}
# If one index works on both nodes, set NCCL_IB_GID_INDEX. If the nodes need
# different indices (e.g. head 4 / worker 3), set them per rank instead —
# both default to NCCL_IB_GID_INDEX when unset.
# NCCL_IB_GID_INDEX=2
# HEAD_GID=4
# WORKER_GID=3

# --- weights -----------------------------------------------------------
# Durable public mirror (same bytes as brandonmusic snapshot 5ab363a8).
# If that Hub id 404s, start.sh downloads MODEL_FALLBACK instead.
MODEL=Mia-AiLab/GLM-5.3-Flash-EXL3-TR3-4bpw
MODEL_FALLBACK=brandonmusic/GLM-5.3-Flash-tr3-4bpw
# Already downloaded the upstream id on this kit? Uncomment so we do not
# re-fetch 164 GiB into a second cache folder:
# MODEL_CACHE_NAME=models--brandonmusic--GLM-5.3-Flash-tr3-4bpw
# Optional: pin a Hub commit on the mirror (empty = branch default).
MODEL_REVISION=25a44fdbf16862a46b7cc9921142c6c81350af2f
# HF cache root on the head (worker uses ${WORKER_HOME}/.cache/huggingface)
# HF_HOME=/home/you/.cache/huggingface
# HF_TOKEN=hf_xxx
# HF CLI override when `hf` lives outside PATH (venv installs). May contain
# arguments. Without it start.sh falls back to `python3 -m
# huggingface_hub.commands.huggingface_cli` when huggingface_hub is importable.
# HF_BIN=/home/you/.hf-cli/venv/bin/hf

# --- serve -------------------------------------------------------------
# Public GHCR image. ./start.sh docker-pulls this on the head, then on
# the worker if that node can reach GHCR; otherwise docker save
# --platform | ssh docker load. No login required.
# Overlay rebuild from this repo: BUILD=1 ./start.sh
# R1 digest pin: pin the exact digest you validated so a restart can never
# silently upgrade. Find yours with:
#   docker image inspect ghcr.io/miaai-lab/glm-5.3-flash-2x-dgx-sparks:exl3 \
#     -f '{{json .RepoDigests}}'
# then set IMAGE to <repo>@<digest> + SKIP_PULL=1. check-updates
# (local/check-updates.sh) compares the registry digest against the pin.
# BUILD=1 with a digest ref is refused by start.sh (cannot tag it).
# Skip the pull (use whatever is already local): SKIP_PULL=1
# Skip copying to the worker: SKIP_SHIP=1
# Force the ~164 GiB rsync even when the worker revision marker matches:
# FORCE_SYNC=1
# Local-only tag (no pull): IMAGE=glm53-flash-sm121:local
IMAGE=ghcr.io/miaai-lab/glm-5.3-flash-2x-dgx-sparks:exl3
SKIP_PULL=0
# GHCR_USER=MiaAI-Lab
# GHCR_TOKEN=ghp_xxx
PORT=8888
TP=2
NNODES=2
MASTER_PORT=29521
QUANTIZATION=exl3
# 0 = CUDA graphs. 1 = eager. start.sh adds capture sizes: DFlash2
# 1 2 4 8 16 24 32, MTP 1 2 3 4 6 8 12 (must include 3).
ENFORCE_EAGER=0
# 1 = fused exllamav3_ext.exl3_moe per layer; 0 = unique-expert LinearEXL3 loop
EXL3_FUSED_MOE=1
# 1 = GPU 128-row tiles for fat prefill experts; 0 = LinearEXL3 fallback
# EXL3_MOE_ROW_TILE=0
# Fused temp rows/expert. 1024 lost the MNBT=1024 A/B (P2b); keep 128.
# EXL3_TEMP_ROWS_FUSED=128
SERVED_MODEL_NAME=GLM-5.3-Flash-EXL3

# Winner on this 2× GB10 kit with DFlash2: fused MoE + DFlash2 k=7.
# Draft KV is auto/bf16; the target still uses KV_CACHE_DTYPE=fp8 (fp8_ds_mla).
# Rollback: SPEC_METHOD=mtp
SPEC_METHOD=dflash
DFLASH_MODEL=incoai/GLM-5.3-Flash-DFlash2
DFLASH_TOKENS=7
# D5: Dynamic Speculative Decoding (vLLM PR #32374, in this image). Empty =
# OFF (static k=DFLASH_TOKENS). Format "start_bs:end_bs:k,..." — draft K per
# concurrency. Validated arm (C7 evidence): k=5 at c>=2 is +5-7% aggregate
# while k=7 stays structured-optimal at c=1.
# DSD_TABLE=1:1:7,2:999:5
# Drafter TP. 2 = measured keep on this 2x GB10 kit (shard the ~2.3 GiB
# DFlash2 drafter across TP; main's C4 keep: idle 8k 938 / decode 65.1).
# 1 = rank 0 only (skip CX7 on a 2.3 GiB draft). Empty = inherit TP.
DFLASH_DRAFT_TP=2
MTP_TOKENS=4
# D4: MTP fallback k=4 (measured 28.6 vs ~24.6 tok/s at k=2 on Entrpi's stack;
# k=5 regresses — pos-5 prose acceptance ~0.23). dflash default unaffected.
MAX_MODEL_LEN=600000  # Operator decision (DSD campaign): 600k window; ~1.6x concurrency margin on the same pool
MAX_NUM_SEQS=4
# R1 bundle (Reederey87-derived, 2026-08-30): 3584 = 14 × 256-token pages —
# page-exact prefill chunks (was D1's 2048). 8192 = known indexer-topk smem
# OOM on this lane. Re-gate with the D1 playbook (boot log budget line +
# memfloor + decode ±3%) before raising further.
MAX_NUM_BATCHED_TOKENS=3584
# R1 bundle: requests above this many prompt tokens take the long-prefill
# scheduling path (chunked prefill / overlap-with-decode). 1792 = 7 pages =
# half the step budget. Emitted by the inner scripts as
# --long-prefill-token-threshold (scheduler flag, OUTSIDE EXTRA_ARGS so an
# arm cannot double-add it). Empty = scheduler default (0 = cap off).
LONG_PREFILL_TOKEN_THRESHOLD=1792
# R1 bundle: async scheduling OFF (Reederey87 A/B: async off ≥ async on at
# c=1 — structured 69.8 vs 67.4). The DSD arm re-enables it explicitly:
#   DSD_TABLE=1:1:7,2:999:5 ASYNC_SCHEDULING=1 ./start.sh restart
# start.sh's dsd_validate refuses DSD_TABLE without ASYNC_SCHEDULING=1.
ASYNC_SCHEDULING=0
# R1 bundle: sparse KDA retention (fork env, read in-process by vLLM):
#   unset/empty = dense checkpoints (default); 0 = retain only the latest
#   completed prompt boundary + shared-prefix junctions; N>0 = interval
#   boundaries. This fork extends it to the SWA/MambaSpec (KDA) groups.
# Forwarded to BOTH ranks only when non-empty (an empty string crashes boot).
VLLM_PREFIX_CACHE_RETENTION_INTERVAL=0
# R1 bundle: FlashInfer JIT workspace INSIDE the mounted vLLM cache so JIT
# kernels survive container recreate (watchdog heals pay no re-JIT).
FLASHINFER_WORKSPACE_BASE=/root/.cache/vllm/flashinfer
GPU_MEM_UTIL=0.85
# C4: pin vLLM's suggested KV budget from the startup log ("Replace
# gpu_memory_utilization config with --kv-cache-memory=N"). Empty = auto.
# Not advisory on GB10 (UMA allocates from MemFree). Overrides GPU_MEM_UTIL.
# D2 (memory-floor methodology, ported from Entrpi): any pin/budget raise
# must be backed by a measured floor — tools/memfloor.sh <label> -- <workload>
# samples both nodes at 1 Hz; keep the binding floor >= 5 GiB. Budget raises
# are NON-LINEAR in floor cost (explicit budgets bypass the profiler reserve)
# and floors age ~1.5-2 GiB/day. See results/ab/memfloor-* and
# docs/COMPARISON-ENTRPI.md.
# KV_CACHE_MEMORY: REJECTED on this kit — three pinned-boot freezes with the
# NVRM NV_ERR_NO_MEMORY kernel signature (17.7 GiB x2 C4, 14.64 GiB R1; see
# results/ab/r1-phase0/freeze-20260830.md). The pin reserves KV upfront from
# MemFree and eats the slack the post-init window (API bring-up + MM warmup)
# needs. AUTO POOL is the default: 963,265 tokens = 1.61x the 600k window.
# A pin requires BOTH this variable AND ALLOW_KV_PIN=1 (hard guard in
# start.sh) plus a measured memfloor artifact (tools/memfloor.sh, D2).
# KV_CACHE_MEMORY=
# KV_CACHE_MEMORY=
# C2: memory ritual before docker run on both nodes (drop_caches, compact,
# swappiness=0 persisted, swap cycle). 1 = skip. Cache-flusher sidecar (25 min)
# during weight load when CACHE_FLUSHER=1. VALIDATED 2026-08-29 (D2 baseline
# boot): keep 1 on this kit — the load window is a dice roll without it
# (MemFree 3.2 GiB idle floor, load pushes it through zero; crash review).
# SKIP_MEM_RITUAL=0
# CACHE_FLUSHER=1

# D4: WEIGHTS_MODE=local (default) | nfs — head reads the worker's HF cache
# over NFS (NFS-paced load avoids the measured head wedge where a local NVMe
# read outruns UMA page-cache reclaim). Opt-in; the local-mode load on this
# kit is healthy (0.85 / 512 / CG_ESTIMATE=0 + cache flusher).
# WEIGHTS_MODE=local
# NFS_PORT=12049

# D4: served thinking default. 1 = thinking on (pre-D4 behavior), 0 = off
# (Entrpi-measured +7% structured acceptance; reasoning moves to
# message.reasoning). Clients can still override per request.
GLM53_DEFAULT_THINKING=1

KV_CACHE_DTYPE=fp8
# 0 = load vision tower (image + video). 1 = language-only.
LANGUAGE_MODEL_ONLY=0
# Skip max-size dummy MM profile at init (that OOM'd this UMA). Keep 1 with vision.
SKIP_MM_PROFILING=1
LIMIT_MM='{"image":4,"video":1}'

# --- abliteration (optional, default off) -----------------------------------
# ABLIT=1 edits self_attn.o_proj at weight-load (overlay/ablit_runtime.py).
# Artifacts in ablit/ come from
# drowzeys/keys-GLM-5.3-Flash-NVFP4-ablit-l15-45-anchorstock (published
# "dealign-oproj-transplant": layers 15-45 edited, 0-14 stay stock safety
# anchors, MTP block included). Restart to toggle; no rebuild needed.
ABLIT=0
# auto = transplant when ablit/transplant/ is populated, else proj
ABLIT_METHOD=auto
# dealign (published recipe) | bf_oproj | absolute path to a custom direction .pt
ABLIT_DIRECTION=dealign
# Inclusive layer range. 45 is the checkpoint MTP block (used when it loads).
ABLIT_LAYERS=15-45
# W' = (I - alpha * r r^T / ||r||^2) W. 1.0 = plain projection;
# 3.0 = published alpha_ref (over-projects — stronger, less coherent).
ABLIT_ALPHA=3.0
# Also edit the MTP block's o_proj when it is loaded (SPEC_METHOD=mtp).
ABLIT_INCLUDE_MTP=1

# --- API auth --------------------------------------------------------------
# OpenAI-compatible bearer token. vLLM reads the VLLM_API_KEY env var natively
# (fallback when --api-key is absent on the CLI), so the key never lands in
# argv / the `non-default args` startup log. Empty = unauthenticated.
# Same single-key semantics as the DeepSeek V4 Flash DSpark deployment.
# VLLM_API_KEY=

# --- JIT caches / boot warmup ----------------------------------------------
# Overlay ~/.triton and ~/.tilelang die on container recreate. These host
# dirs are bind-mounted to /root/.triton/cache and /root/.tilelang/cache.
# TRITON_HOST_CACHE=
# TILELANG_HOST_CACHE=
# After /health, burn DFlash2 BLOCK / sampler / kpool shapes so TP=2 does
# not JIT mid-collective. 0 = skip (nonfatal either way).
GLM53_BOOT_SHAPE_WARMUP=1
# GLM53_WARMUP_REQ_TIMEOUT=240
# Suppress client stop strings until </think> (thinking-on default). 0 = off.
GLM53_SUPPRESS_STOPS_IN_REASONING=1
# When a decode seq is running, do not mix a peer prefill into that step
# (issue #6). skip = decode-only steps; N>0 = cap mixed prefill tokens; 0 = off.
GLM53_MIXED_PREFILL_CHUNK=1024
# EngineCore execute timeout (seconds). Stock 300 is short for a cold JIT.
# VLLM_EXECUTE_MODEL_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=1800

# Host NCCL preload. Default off: the glm53-flash image already has nvidia-nccl,
# and LD_PRELOAD of a second SO makes DeepEP assert duplicate NCCL.
USE_HOST_NCCL=0
# NCCL_HOST_DIR=/home/you/nccl-2.30.7
# WORKER_NCCL_HOST_DIR=/home/you/nccl-2.30.7
NCCL_SO_NAME=libnccl.so.2.30.7
NCCL_IB_GID_INDEX=3
# vLLM deducts a CUDA-graph memory estimate from the KV pool. Where the estimate
# exceeds what the graphs actually use, 0 returns that memory to KV with graphs
# still enabled. 1 = upstream default.
CG_ESTIMATE=1
# 2026-08-29 crash review: this kit runs CG_ESTIMATE=0 (returns the ~1.4-2.4 GiB
# CUDA-graph memory estimate to the KV pool; graphs stay ON). With =0, 1M fits at
# GPU_MEM_UTIL=0.85 without a pin. Never set GPU_MEM_UTIL > 0.85 (start.sh refuses:
# >0.85 froze both nodes via UVM livelock). Never pin KV_CACHE_MEMORY above the
# profiled 'to-fit' value without CG_ESTIMATE=0 + cache flusher.
# MEMFREE_ALARM_KB=8388608   (fleet_watchdog MemFree floor alarm; default 8 GiB)
NCCL_DEBUG=WARN
